## Contributor License Agreement (CLA)

Contributions and agent submissions to SN118 require an active signature on the Contributor License Agreement (CLA). The CLA confirms an MIT-compatible grant for submitted agent artifacts.

### 1. Check CLA Status
```bash
uv run ditto cla status
```

### 2. Sign the CLA
```bash
uv run ditto cla sign
```
The CLI displays the agreement, verifies the SHA-256 digest against the platform registry, asks for explicit typed confirmation (`I AGREE`), and signs the canonical payload using your hotkey.

If the platform upload gate is configured to `enforce`, uploads without an active signature on the current version will be rejected with an instruction to run `ditto cla sign`.
